> MY QUESTION:  how do the experts get to level 20?  through extensive
> combat or just incubi?

Many experts don't - generally combat characters are better staying 
slightly lower level, as they will meet easier monsters. Once you can hit 
all monsters every time, the only advantage for combat-oriented characters 
is hit points, which are in any case easier to increase in other ways. I 
just did a wizmode experiment and a con 18 Valk got 219 HP at level 30 - 
I've usually ascended combat characters between level 16 & 18 with 400+ HP.

Users of magic go higher because it can reduce the failure chance of their 
spells, increases mana (which is not as easy to increase in other ways as 
HP), and the most important spell's damage increases with level so the 
increased difficulty of opponents is offset.

In a normal ascension, you only tend to kill enough monsters to get to 
around 17th level. If you want to go higher, you need to find alternate 
means - you've found two, but there is a bottled version as well.

